      When executing <strong>vscode remove duplicate lines</strong> tasks, standard installations provide sorting tools in the Command Palette (<code>Sort Lines Ascending</code>), but rely on dedicated marketplace extensions (such as <em>Filter Lines</em> or <em>Unique Lines</em>) to wipe duplicate rows while retaining original document structure. Running <strong>vs code remove duplicate lines</strong> operations on files containing hundreds of thousands of lines can occasionally cause temporary editor freezes.
